{% comment %}Approved industry-story homepage. Original homepage remains available through index.original.json.{% endcomment %}
{% for block in section.blocks %}
{% assign signup_instance = section.id | append: '-' | append: block.id %}
{% case block.type %}
{% when 'hero' %}
<section class="story-section story-section--hero" id="story-intro" aria-labelledby="story-intro-title" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
<div class="story-container">
<h1 class="story-heading story-heading--hero" id="story-intro-title"><span class="story-hero__first">{{ block.settings.headline | escape }}</span><em>{{ block.settings.close | escape }}</em></h1>
<div class="story-copy story-hero__intro">{{ block.settings.intro }}</div>
{% render 'inchy-story-signup', instance_id: signup_instance %}
<p class="story-note">{{ block.settings.note | escape }}</p>
</div>
</section>
{% when 'pouch' %}
<section class="story-section story-section--pouch" id="product" aria-labelledby="product-title" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
<div class="story-container">
<div class="story-product-grid">
<div class="story-product-visual">{% render 'inchy-packaging', image_class: 'story-packaging', loading: 'eager' %}</div>
<div class="story-product-copy" id="shop-inchy">
<p class="story-kicker">{{ block.settings.heading | escape }}</p>
<h2 class="story-heading" id="product-title"><span>One seed.</span><span>Protein and fibre.</span></h2>
<p class="story-pouch-position">Nonpharmaceutical satiety</p>
<div class="story-copy">{{ block.settings.copy }}</div>
{% capture story_product_url %}{% render 'inchy-shop-url' %}{% endcapture %}
<a class="story-text-link" href="{{ story_product_url | strip | escape }}">Explore FORM1</a>
<a class="story-button story-product-access" href="#first-access">Get first access</a>
</div>
</div>
<dl class="story-stats">
<div><dt>kcal per 30 g</dt><dd>{{ block.settings.calories | escape }}</dd></div>
<div><dt>protein</dt><dd>{{ block.settings.protein | escape }}</dd></div>
<div><dt>fibre</dt><dd>{{ block.settings.fibre | escape }}</dd></div>
<div><dt>additives</dt><dd>{{ block.settings.additives | escape }}</dd></div>
</dl>
</div>
</section>
{% when 'founder' %}
<section class="story-section story-section--founder" aria-label="A founder's conviction" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
<div class="story-container"><figure class="story-founder-bet"><blockquote><p>“Everyone's betting the answer to appetite is an injection. I'm betting it's a seed.”</p></blockquote><figcaption>— Russell White, founder</figcaption></figure></div>
</section>
{% when 'problem' %}
<section class="story-section story-section--problem" id="approach" aria-labelledby="approach-title" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
<div class="story-container">
<p class="story-kicker">Common problem</p>
<div class="story-split"><h2 class="story-heading" id="approach-title"><span>Dinner ends.</span><span>The wanting doesn't.</span></h2>
<div class="story-copy">
<p>10pm. The kitchen is closed and you're back in it. One biscuit becomes three. Then the morning-after audit. If that loop sounds familiar, you already understand why INCHY exists.</p>
</div></div>
<hr class="story-divider">
<p class="story-kicker">Our approach</p>
<div class="story-split"><div><h3 class="story-heading story-approach-heading">Put satiety first.</h3><a class="story-text-link" href="{{ routes.root_url }}#process">Explore the approach</a></div><div class="story-copy"><p>Satiety is the fullness that lasts after eating. Most of this industry designs for taste, speed and shelf price, and lets fullness fall where it falls. We put satiety first and made everything else negotiate with it.</p></div></div>
</div>
</section>
{% when 'refusal' %}
<section class="story-section story-section--refusal" id="process" aria-labelledby="process-title" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
<div class="story-container">
<p class="story-kicker">The formulation</p>
<h2 class="story-heading" id="process-title"><span>What's in the pouch: sacha inchi.</span><span>What isn't: everything else.</span></h2>
<div class="story-refusal story-copy">
<p><strong>The invention is what the seed becomes.</strong></p>
<p>Sacha inchi was already pressed for oil and sold as flour. But the seed's earthy taste and texture could dominate the food it was added to. Keeping its protein and fibre together was only half the challenge. Making that combination work in everyday food was the other half.</p>
<p>Our process gives that combination a new expression: FORM1. Protein and fibre from the same seed, with a more neutral taste and a texture made to mix into food people already eat. Nothing added to mask it. The method stays ours; the difference belongs in your bowl.</p>
<p><strong>The easy versions existed.</strong></p>
<p>Isolate the protein. Strip the fibre. Cover the taste with vanilla and sweetener — we had a supplier ready to do it. We refused all of it.</p>
<p><strong>No sweeteners. No flavours. No additives.</strong></p>
<p class="story-refusal-close">Not because we couldn't.<br>Because we wouldn't.</p>
<a class="story-text-link" href="{{ routes.root_url }}?view=process">Explore our process</a>
</div>
</div>
</section>
{% when 'industry' %}
<section class="story-section story-section--industry" id="origin" aria-labelledby="origin-title" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
<div class="story-container">
<p class="story-kicker">Our origin</p>
<h2 class="story-heading" id="origin-title"><span>The industry that</span><span>didn't exist.</span></h2>
<div class="story-industry-grid"><div class="story-copy">{{ block.settings.copy }}</div><figure class="story-grower"><img src="{{ 'inchy-growers-harvest.jpg' | asset_url }}" width="1280" height="854" alt="Emilio holding harvested sacha inchi fruit in the field" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Emilio, one of our growers in northeast Colombia.</figcaption></figure></div>
<p class="story-industry__statement">One company, building two things: the nutraceutical, and the industry that grows it.</p>
{% comment %}Future verified metric: families under signed contract. Add only after contracts are signed; never show an estimated or placeholder count. Association's full legal name stays off the page until registration is confirmed.{% endcomment %}
<p class="story-industry__follow">This is being built in public. Watch it happen: <a href="{{ block.settings.founder_url | default: 'https://www.instagram.com/reluctantruss/' }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">@reluctantruss<span class="story-sr"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a></p>
</div>
</section>
{% when 'research' %}
<section class="story-section story-section--research" id="research" aria-labelledby="research-title" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
<div class="story-container">
<p class="story-kicker">The research</p>
<h2 class="story-heading" id="research-title"><span>What the research shows.</span><span>And what it doesn't.</span></h2>
<div class="story-research-grid">
<div class="story-research-item">
<p class="story-kicker">Nutrient research</p>
<h3>Protein + fibre</h3>
<p>Protein and certain dietary fibres can stimulate the body's own release of GLP-1 — a gut hormone involved in appetite regulation.</p>
<p class="story-evidence-limit">These are findings about particular nutrients and study preparations. They do not establish the GLP-1 response to a serving of INCHY.</p>
<a class="story-text-link" href="{{ routes.root_url }}?view=research#protein">Protein + fibre evidence</a>
</div>
<div class="story-research-item">
<p class="story-kicker">Laboratory research</p>
<h3>Sacha inchi peptides</h3>
<p>In laboratory tests, peptides derived from sacha inchi inhibited DPP-IV, the enzyme that breaks down GLP-1. (Zhang et al., 2023.)</p>
<p class="story-evidence-limit">A laboratory study — not a human trial of finished INCHY. It does not establish effects on appetite or GLP-1 in people.</p>
<a class="story-text-link" href="{{ routes.root_url }}?view=research">Explore the evidence</a>
</div>
</div>
<p class="story-copy story-research-close">We publish the boundaries of the evidence on purpose. A category built on satiety has to be more careful than one built on hype.</p>
</div>
</section>
{% when 'routine' %}
<section class="story-section story-section--routine" id="routine" aria-labelledby="routine-title" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
<div class="story-container">
<p class="story-kicker">The routine</p>
<h2 class="story-heading" id="routine-title">Make it part of the day.</h2>
<div class="story-routine-grid">{% for step in (1..3) %}<figure class="story-routine-step story-routine-step--{{ step }}"><div class="story-routine-photo"><img src="{{ 'inchy-routine.jpg' | asset_url }}" width="1942" height="809" loading="lazy" alt="{% case step %}{% when 1 %}Powder added to yoghurt{% when 2 %}Powder added to oats{% when 3 %}Powder stirred into a drink{% endcase %}"></div><figcaption><span>0{{ step }}</span>{% case step %}{% when 1 %}In yoghurt{% when 2 %}In oats{% when 3 %}In a drink{% endcase %}</figcaption></figure>{% endfor %}</div>
<p class="story-copy">Measure the serving stated on the pouch. Mix thoroughly. Get on with your day.</p>
<a class="story-text-link" href="{{ routes.root_url }}?view=how-to-use">Find your routine</a>
</div>
</section>
{% when 'faq' %}
<section class="story-section story-section--faq" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
<div class="story-container story-faq-grid">
<h2 class="story-heading" id="faq-title"><span>Questions, answered</span><span>straight.</span></h2>
<div class="story-faq">
<details><summary>How is INCHY different from a protein isolate?<span class="story-faq__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="story-faq__answer"><p>A protein isolate is processed to concentrate protein, usually removing much of the other seed material. INCHY keeps protein and fibre from the same seed together in one preparation. Its focus is satiety and everyday use, rather than protein content alone.</p></div></details>
<details><summary>What does it taste like?<span class="story-faq__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="story-faq__answer"><p>Unflavoured means no added flavour. Sacha inchi still has its own taste and texture, which can come through depending on what you mix it with.</p></div></details>
<details><summary>Is INCHY a GLP-1 medicine?<span class="story-faq__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="story-faq__answer"><p>INCHY is a sacha inchi nutraceutical powder, not a GLP-1 medicine. Our <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}?view=research">research guide</a> explains the ingredient research and what it does and does not establish about finished INCHY.</p></div></details>
<details><summary>Why a growers association?<span class="story-faq__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="story-faq__answer">{{ block.settings.association_answer }}</div></details>
</div>
</div>
</section>
{% when 'launch' %}
<section class="story-section story-section--close" id="first-access" aria-labelledby="first-access-title" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
<div class="story-container story-close-grid">
<h2 class="story-heading" id="first-access-title"><span>Eat. Feel enough.</span><span>Go live.</span></h2>
<div>
<p class="story-close__intro">Be first when FORM1 opens for U.S. orders.</p>
{% render 'inchy-story-signup', instance_id: signup_instance %}
</div>
</div>
</section>
{% endcase %}
{% endfor %}
