          "id": "copy",
          "label": "Industry story",
          "default": "<p>Sacha inchi has 3,000 years of use behind it. It was already grown, pressed, traded and sold. But the crop under this company had no organised industry to build on: no shared standard for what good looks like, no dependable purchasing a farmer could plan around.</p><p>So we're building it. A growers association in northeast Colombia. Seed bought direct, from farmers we know by name. A crop formalised — and a reason to plant again next year.</p>"
